Final reciprocal isoform-switch support diagnostic
Input: terminal Kallisto abundances against GENCODE v47 human transcripts
A switch is reciprocal when one transcript has <=0.5 estimated counts in B and the other has <=0.5 in A; support is the smaller enriched-sample count.
The balance filter is max(sample A/B gene counts) / min(sample A/B gene counts) <=1.25, to focus on isoform usage rather than total-gene changes.
